# 12. MODULE NINE: ADVIBE SERVICE CATALOGUE AND AI KNOWLEDGE BASE

## 12.1 Purpose

The AI needs accurate information about AdVibe before it can recommend services or generate meaningful outreach.

Build a central service catalogue.

Do not hard-code service descriptions or prices into individual prompts or application components.

The administrator must be able to edit service information from the settings area.

## 12.2 Initial Service Categories

### 1. Product Advertisements
AI-powered advertisements for physical products.

### 2. Service Advertisements
Videos explaining and promoting business services.

### 3. UGC-Style Advertisements
Creator-style product and service promotional videos.

### 4. Explainer Videos
Videos designed to explain products, services, processes or business propositions.

### 5. Event and Campaign Advertisements
Promotional content for events, campaigns, launches and special announcements.

### 6. Brand Videos
Videos communicating a company's identity, story and value proposition.

### 7. Monthly AI Video Content Retainers
Recurring monthly production for businesses requiring consistent promotional content.

### 8. AI Promotional Mini-Series
Cinematic branded entertainment designed to build attention and audience engagement through episodic storytelling.

### 9. AI Video Directing Training Academy
Training for people who want to learn AI video creation and directing.

Additional service categories must be configurable.

## 12.3 Service Recommendation Logic

The AI should match businesses with appropriate services.

Examples:

| Prospect type | Possible recommendation |
|---|---|
