# 13. MODULE TEN: CAMPAIGN STUDIO

## 13.1 Purpose

Campaign Studio should allow AdVibe to create personalised outreach campaigns for selected businesses.

It must support individual prospecting and eligible bulk campaign preparation.

## 13.2 Campaign Types

- Cold business introduction.
- Product advertisement offer.
- Monthly content retainer offer.
- White-label agency partnership.
- AI promotional mini-series offer.
- Explainer video offer.
- Training Academy promotion.
- Dream 100 relationship-building campaign.
- Event or seasonal campaign.
- Custom campaign.

## 13.3 Campaign Creation Workflow

1. Create a campaign.
2. Give it a name.
3. Select target businesses.
4. Select contacts.
5. Choose country and industry filters.
6. Choose the service being promoted.
7. Choose the outreach objective.
8. Define the desired tone.
9. Select an email template or generate a new one.
10. AI researches and personalises each message.
11. Review messages individually or in a batch.
12. Approve selected messages.
13. Create individual Gmail drafts.
14. Synchronise sending status when supported.
15. Track engagement.
16. Manage follow-ups.

## 13.4 Personalisation Requirements

Every generated email should consider:

- Business name.
- Contact name, if reliably known.
- Business category.
- Products or services.
- Relevant marketing activity.
- Evidence from research.
- Potential creative opportunity.
- Recommended AdVibe service.
- Country-specific pricing where appropriate.
- Campaign objective.

The AI must avoid:

- Generic mass email language.
- Fabricated compliments.
- False claims of familiarity.
- Pretending to have spoken to someone.
- Unsubstantiated claims about a company's marketing performance.
- Fake personalisation.
- Overly aggressive sales language.

## 13.5 Individual Email Approval

This is a strict requirement.

The system must create individual email drafts, not one email with multiple prospects in the recipient list.

The user must be able to:

- Review each email.
- Edit the subject.
- Edit the body.
- Regenerate the email.
- Approve the email.
- Reject the email.
- Create its Gmail draft.
- View the Gmail draft reference.
- Record when it is sent.

Bulk selection may be used to prepare multiple drafts, but each recipient must have a separate personalised message.

**The application must not automatically send prospecting emails without explicit authorisation and a separately configured sending policy.**

