# 15. MODULE TWELVE: EMAIL TRACKING AND PERFORMANCE ANALYTICS

## 15.1 Purpose

The application should measure the performance of AdVibe's email outreach and campaigns.

It must distinguish between individual prospect engagement and campaign-level statistics.

## 15.2 Metrics

Track:

- Drafts created.
- Emails confirmed as sent.
- Delivery status where available.
- Estimated opens.
- Unique opens.
- Total link clicks.
- Unique link clicks.
- Click-through rate.
- Replies.
- Positive replies.
- Bounces.
- Unsubscribes.
- Meetings booked.
- Proposals requested.
- Converted customers.

## 15.3 Open Tracking

Where permitted and enabled, use a unique tracking pixel per recipient and message.

Record:

- Message identifier.
- Contact identifier.
- First recorded open.
- Total recorded open events.
- Last recorded open.
- Campaign.

Label the metric "Estimated opens".

Explain that privacy protections, automated image loading and security scanners can produce inaccurate results.

Never present opens as proof that a human read the message.

## 15.4 Click Tracking

Use unique tracking links for supported outbound links.

Example:

A prospect receives a personalised email containing an AdVibe portfolio link.

The link should be associated with:

- Business.
- Contact.
- Campaign.
- Email.
- Destination URL.

When clicked, record the click and redirect to the approved destination.

Support:

- Portfolio link.
- Service page.
- Case study.
- Booking page.
- Other approved destination.

Track unique clickers separately from total clicks.

Protect against duplicate events and automated link-scanning bots.

Do not rewrite or obscure links in a way that creates misleading destinations.

## 15.5 Reply Tracking

Where Gmail mailbox synchronisation is authorised, track:

- Reply received.
- Reply date.
- Reply thread.
- Contact.
- Campaign.
- Reply classification.

AI may classify replies as:

- Positive.
- Interested.
- Request for information.
- Pricing request.
- Meeting request.
- Not interested.
- Referral.
- Out of office.
- Unclear.

AI classifications must be reviewable and editable.

## 15.6 Campaign Analytics

Provide:

- Sent volume.
- Delivery rate where available.
- Estimated open rate.
- Unique click-through rate.
- Reply rate.
- Positive reply rate.
- Bounce rate.
- Unsubscribe rate.
- Meeting conversion.
- Opportunity conversion.
- Revenue attributed to campaign where known.

Use clearly defined denominators for every percentage.

Do not combine Gmail data and SendFox data into one statistic unless their definitions and reporting periods are compatible.

